### pitchwire, by hand
#
# Every read endpoint, in the order somebody would actually meet them. Works in the VS Code REST
# Client, in Rider and in Visual Studio. Bring the stack up first:
#
#   docker compose up -d --wait
#
# The ingest endpoints are not here. They need an HMAC over a length prefixed timestamp and body, and
# a request file cannot compute one. The feed does it in `RequestSigner`, and the integration tests
# do it against a real host, which is a better example than a signature pasted into a comment would
# be.

@api = http://localhost:5080

### Is it up
GET {{api}}/health/ready

### Countries, and how many competitions each one has
GET {{api}}/countries

### The competitions in one country, top flight first
GET {{api}}/countries/england/leagues

### Everything being played right now
# The envelope is `value` plus `nextLink`. `$top` defaults to 50 and is capped at 100.
GET {{api}}/matches/live?$top=10

### One match: the score, the timeline, both team sheets and the statistics
# Take an id from the live list above.
@matchId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{api}}/matches/{{matchId}}

### The events of a match from a sequence onwards
# What a client asks for after a dropped connection, rather than refetching the whole match.
GET {{api}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events?from=0

### The seasons currently being played
GET {{api}}/seasons

### The fixture list
# `nextLink` in the response carries the `$skiptoken` for the next page. There is no `$skip`.
@seasonId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}/fixtures?$top=5

### One season: its participating teams and the rounds actually on its schedule
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}

### Fixtures for one team in one round
@teamId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}/fixtures?round=1&teamId={{teamId}}&$top=5

### The next page
# Paste the token from the `nextLink` above.
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}/fixtures?$top=5&$skiptoken=

### Results, newest first
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}/results?$top=5

### Finished matches for the same team and round
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}/results?round=1&teamId={{teamId}}&$top=5

### The league table
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}/table

### The scorers
GET {{api}}/seasons/{{seasonId}}/scorers?$top=10

### A team's recent form
GET {{api}}/teams/{{teamId}}/form?seasonId={{seasonId}}&count=5

### This browser's identity
# 401 until this client has registered, which is a normal answer rather than an error.
GET {{api}}/devices/me

### Register this browser
POST {{api}}/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Follow some teams
# Replaces the whole list. Send an empty array to follow nobody.
PUT {{api}}/devices/me/favourites
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "teamIds": ["{{teamId}}"]
}

### Set what to be told about, and when
PUT {{api}}/devices/me/preferences
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timeZoneId": "Europe/Istanbul",
  "quietHoursStart": "23:00:00",
  "quietHoursEnd": "08:00:00",
  "notifyOnGoal": true,
  "notifyOnRedCard": false,
  "notifyOnKickoff": false,
  "notifyOnFullTime": true
}

### The public key a browser needs to subscribe to push
GET {{api}}/push/public-key

### The OpenAPI document
# The browser types are generated from this, and a CI job fails if the two have drifted apart. There
# is a readable version of the same thing at http://localhost:5080/scalar/v1
GET {{api}}/openapi/v1.json
